print of "=== HALTING: RUNAWAY LOOP CONTRACT (#861) ==="
print of "--- HD1: bare-predicate loop around a runaway exits via STALL ---"
# Pre-#861 this loop "terminated" via the defect: H(x) fell under h_low as x
# doubled, every clause of the entropy `converged` was met, and the loop
# exited after ~13 iterations reporting the canonical instability as
# converged. Now `converged` (value-routed) refuses a runaway, and the
# stall backstop ends the loop after 100 quiet, non-finite or diverging iterations with the
# honest exit reason.

counter is 0
x is 10.0
x is 10.0

loop while not converged:
    counter is counter + 1
    x is x * 2.0

print of counter
print of report of x
print of __loop_exit__
print of why is x

print of ""
print of "--- HD1b: additive quiet-relative runaway also stalls ---"
counter is 0
x is 1000000.0
x is 1000000.0
loop while not converged:
    counter is counter + 1
    x is x + 200.0
print of counter
print of report of x
print of __loop_exit__
print of why is x
print of ""
assert of [counter == 100, "HD1b loop iteration count"]
assert of [__loop_exit__ == "stalled", "HD1b stall exit"]
print of "=== RUNAWAY LOOP CONTRACT COMPLETE ==="
